I found the issue! You have sanitizeText defined twice - once outside exportToPDF and once inside. But the one inside is causing a problem because of where it's placed.

The Problem:

Look at your code structure - you have:

1. External sanitizeText (outside exportToPDF) - this one is fine
2. Internal sanitizeText (inside exportToPDF at the top) - THIS is the problem

The issue is that you defined the internal sanitizeText BEFORE the addWrappedText function, but you also have another sanitizeText inside addWrappedText? Actually, looking carefully, addWrappedText is calling sanitizeText(text) but the function is defined after it in the code flow.

The Fix - Remove the duplicate internal definitions:

Delete these lines from inside your exportToPDF function (the ones right after try {):

```javascript
        // ALL helper functions defined first
        function sanitizeText(text) {
            if (!text || typeof text !== 'string') return '';
            return text.replace(/[^\x20-\x7E\u00A0-\u00FF]/g, '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
        }
        
        function formatDateStr(dateString, format = 'full') {
            if (!dateString) return 'Not specified';
            try {
                const date = new Date(dateString);
                if (isNaN(date.getTime())) return dateString;
                const day = date.getDate().toString().padStart(2, '0');
                const month = (date.getMonth() + 1).toString().padStart(2, '0');
                const year = date.getFullYear();
                if (format === 'short') return `${day}/${month}`;
                return `${day}/${month}/${year}`;
            } catch (e) {
                return dateString;
            }
        }
        
